---
config:
  layout: elk
  elk:
    nodePlacementStrategy: BRANDES_KOEPF
---
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Initial
    
    Initial: MessageStore(A): [M1, M2, M3]<br><br>MessageStore(B): [M1]<br><br>NodeState(A↦B): {messages: [M1,M2,M3], offers: [], requests: []}<br><br>NodeState(B↦A): {messages: [M1], offers: [], requests: []}
    
    Initial --> Idle: Initialisation of the protocol is complete, both Alice and Bob are ready to send and receive messages.

    note left of Idle
        Either Alice or Bob can add messages to the payload and send them to the other party. The other party can then receive the payload, store the messages, and acknowledge them. This process can be repeated until all messages have been sent and acknowledged.
    end note

    Idle: Alice and Bob are idle, waiting for messages to be sent or received
    
    Idle --> AliceAddMessages: Alice adds messages to payload

    Idle --> Idle: No action is taken, Alice and Bob remain idle
    
    AliceAddMessages: Payload(A↦B): {messages: [M1, M2, M3], acks: []}

    AliceAddMessages --> AliceSend: Alice sends payload
    
    AliceSend: PayloadSent(A↦B): true<br><br>PayloadReceived(B↦A): false
    
    AliceSend --> AliceSendPayloadInTransit: Sent payload from Alice to Bob is in transit

    AliceSendPayloadInTransit: Sent payload from Alice to Bob is in transit

    AliceSendPayloadInTransit --> BobReceive: Bob receives payload
    
    BobReceive: PayloadSent(A↦B): true<br><br>PayloadReceived(B↦A): true

    BobReceive --> ReceiverProcessing

    state ReceiverProcessing {
        note  left of BobStoresMessages
            Bob notices that Alice has sent M1 thus that doesn't need to be sent to Alice.
        end note

        BobStoresMessages: MessageStore(A): [M1, M2, M3]<br><br>MessageStore(B): [M1, M2, M3]<br><br>NodeState(A↦B): {messages: [M1,M2,M3], offers: [], requests: []}<br><br>NodeState(B↦A): {messages: [], offers: [], requests: []}

        [*] --> BobStoresMessages: Bob stores messages
        BobStoresMessages --> [*]

        --
        note left of BobDetermineAck
            Bob acknowledges all messages they received from Alice to indicate that they have received 
            them. This is done by editing the existing payload to include the ACKs for the messages 
            received from Alice.
        end note
        
        BobDetermineAck:  Payload(A↦B): {messages: [M1, M2, M3], acks: [M1, M2, M3]}

        [*] --> BobDetermineAck: Bob acknowledges messages received from Alice
        BobDetermineAck --> [*]
    }
    
    ReceiverProcessing --> BobSend: Bob sends acks
    
    BobSend: PayloadSent(A↦B): false<br><br>PayloadReceived(B↦A): false<br><br>PayloadSent(B↦A): true<br><br>PayloadReceived(A↦B): false
    
    BobSend --> BobSendPayloadInTransit: Sent payload from Bob to Alice is in transit

    BobSendPayloadInTransit: Sent payload from Bob to Alice is in transit

    BobSendPayloadInTransit --> AliceReceiveAck: Alice receives acks

    note right of AliceReceiveAck
        Alice notices that Bob has acknowledged M1, M2, and M3 thus that doesn't need to be sent to Bob. Therefore, Alice can remove it from the NodeState.
    end note

    AliceReceiveAck: PayloadSent(B↦A): true<br><br>PayloadReceived(A↦B): true<br><br>NodeState(A↦B): {messages: [], offers: [], requests: []}<br><br>NodeState(B↦A): {messages: [], offers: [], requests: []}
    
    AliceReceiveAck --> [*]
